  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 335 AM CDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nA shortwave trough situated over the Central Plains will continue \nmoving slowly eastward as we move into the day. Some lingering \nshowers and sprinkles this morning will gradually diminish with \nclearing from west to east as we move into the late morning and \nearly afternoon hours. Abundant afternoon insolation will result in \nabove average temperatures with maximum temperatures climbing into \nthe 70s areawide. Normal highs for late October are in the upper 60s.\n\nThu-Sat...a narrow mid/upper ridge will continue to impact the area \nthrough Saturday bringing above average temperatures and dry weather \nconditions. This ridge will gradually translate eastward into the \nMississippi Valley area while a robust mid/upper trough just off the \nCA coast today will gradually build eastward into the Central Great \nBasin area and the Southwest. As we move into Saturday, the entrance \nregion to the H25 jet will gradually build into the Central High \nPlains bringing increasing chances for showers to much of western \nand parts of central KS late in the period.\n\nHigher probabilities for showers are expected to arrive Sunday night \ninto Monday night as the pv anomaly accelerates over the Central \nPlains region and a cold front arrives ushering in cooler more \nseasonable air for Monday-Tuesday. Below average temperatures are \nexpected in the wake of the front with highs on Tue struggling to \nclimb out of the 50s over parts of central KS.",
